H500.definition:
or (more properly) אֶלְעָלֵה; from H410 (אֵל) and H5927 (עָלָה); God (is) going up;
Elale or Elaleh, a place east of the Jordan
KJV: Elealeh.

H501.definition:
from H410 (אֵל) and H6213 (עָשָׂה); God has made;
Elasah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Elasah, Eleasah.

H502.definition:
a primitive root, to associate with;
hence, to learn (and causatively to teach)
KJV: learn, teach, utter.

H503.definition:
denominative from H505 (אֶלֶף);
causative, to make athousandfold
KJV: bring forth thousands.

H504.definition:
from H502 (אָלַף);
a family; also (from the sense of yoking or taming) an ox or cow
KJV: family, kine, oxen.

H505.definition:
prop, the same as H504 (אֶלֶף);
hence (the ox's head being the first letter of the alphabet, and this eventually used as a numeral) a thousand
KJV: thousand.

H506.definition:
(Aramaic) or אֶלֶף; (Aramaic), corresponding to H505 (אֶלֶף)
{hence (the ox's head being the first letter of the alphabet, and this eventually used as a numeral) a thousand}
KJV: thousand.

H507.definition:
the same as H505 (אֶלֶף);
Eleph, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eleph.

H508.definition:
from H410 (אֵל) and H6466 (פָּעַל); God (is) act;
Elpaal, an Israelite
KJV: Elpaal.

H509.definition:
a primitive root;
to press
KJV: urge.

H510.definition:
probably from H408 (אַל) and H6965 (קוּם);
a non-rising (i.e. resistlessness)
KJV: no rising up.

H511.definition:
from H410 (אֵל) and H7069 (קָנָה); God has obtained;
Elkanah, the name of several Israelites
KJV: Elkanah.

H512.definition:
patrial from a name of uncertain derivation;
an Elkoshite or native of Elkosh
KJV: Elkoshite.

H513.definition:
probably from H410 (אֵל) and a masculine form of H8435 (תּוֹלְדָה) (compare H8434 (תּוֹלָד)); God (is) generator;
Eltolad, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eltolad.

H514.definition:
or (more properly) אֶלְתְּקֵה; of uncertain derivation;
Eltekeh or Elteke, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eltekeh.

H515.definition:
from H410 (אֵל) and H8626 (תָּקַן); God (is) straight;
Eltekon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Eltekon.

H516.definition:
from H408 (אַל) and H7843 (שָׁחַת);
'Thou must not destroy'; probably the opening words to a popular song
KJV: Al-taschith.

H517.definition:
a primitive word;
a mother (as the bond of the family); in a wide sense (both literally and figuratively (like father))
KJV: dam, mother, [idiom] parting.

H518.definition:
a primitive particle;
used very widely as demonstrative, lo!; interrogative, whether?; or conditional, if, although; also Oh that!, when; hence, as a negative, not
KJV: (and, can-, doubtless, if, that) (not), [phrase] but, either, [phrase] except, [phrase] more(-over if, than), neither, nevertheless, nor, oh that, or, [phrase] save (only, -ing), seeing, since, sith, [phrase] surely (no more, none, not), though, [phrase] of a truth, [phrase] unless, [phrase] verily, when, whereas, whether, while, [phrase] yet.

H519.definition:
apparently a primitive word;
a maidservant or female slave
KJV: (hand-) bondmaid(-woman), maid(-servant).

H520.definition:
prolonged from H517 (אֵם);
properly, a mother (i.e. unit of measure, or the fore-arm (below the elbow), i.e. a cubit; also a door-base (as a bond of the entrance)
KJV: cubit, [phrase] hundred (by exchange for H3967 (מֵאָה)), measure, post.

H521.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H520 (אַמָּה)
{properly, a mother (i.e. unit of measure, or the fore-arm (below the elbow), i.e. a cubit; also a door-base (as a bond of the entrance)}
KJV: cubit.

H522.definition:
the same as H520 (אַמָּה);
Ammah, a hill in Palestine
KJV: Ammah.

H523.definition:
from the same as H517 (אֵם);
a collection, i.e. community of persons
KJV: nation, people.

H524.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H523 (אֻמַּה)
{a collection, i.e. community of persons}
KJV: nation.

H525.definition:
from H539 (אָמַן), probably in the sense of training; like H542 (אָמָן)
skilled, i.e. an architect
KJV: one brought up.

H526.definition:
the same as H525 (אָמוֹן);
Amon, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Amon.

H527.definition:
a variation for H1995 (הָמוֹן);
a throng of people
KJV: multitude.

H529.definition:
from H539 (אָמַן);
established, i.e. (figuratively) trusty; also (abstractly) trustworthiness
KJV: faith(-ful), truth.

H530.definition:
or (shortened) אֱמֻנָה; feminine of H529 (אֵמוּן);
literally firmness; figuratively security; morally fidelity
KJV: faith(-ful, -ly, -ness, (man)), set office, stability, steady, truly, truth, verily.

H531.definition:
from H553 (אָמַץ); strong;
Amots, an Israelite
KJV: Amoz.

H532.definition:
an abbreviated form for H526 (אָמוֹן);
Ami, an Israelite
KJV: Ami.

H533.definition:
or (shortened) אַמִּץ; from H553 (אָמַץ);
strong or (abstractly) strength
KJV: courageous, mighty, strong (one).

H534.definition:
apparently from H559 (אָמַר) (in the sense of self-exaltation);
a summit (of a tree or mountain
KJV: bough, branch.

H535.definition:
a primitive root;
to droop; by implication to be sick, to mourn
KJV: languish, be weak, wax feeble.

H538.definition:
from H517 (אֵם); gathering-spot;
Amam, a place in Palestine
KJV: Amam.

H539.definition:
a primitive root; (Isaiah 30:21; interchangeable with H541 (אָמַן), to go to the right hand)
properly, to build up or support; to foster as a parent or nurse; figuratively to render (or be) firm or faithful, to trust or believe, to be permanent or quiet; morally to be true or certain;
KJV: hence, assurance, believe, bring up, establish, [phrase] fail, be faithful (of long continuance, stedfast, sure, surely, trusty, verified), nurse, (-ing father), (put), trust, turn to the right.

H540.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H539 (אָמַן)
{properly, to build up or support; to foster as a parent or nurse; figuratively to render (or be) firm or faithful, to trust or believe, to be permanent or quiet; morally to be true or certain};
KJV: believe, faithful, sure.

H541.definition:
denominative from H3225 (יָמִין);
to take the right hand road
KJV: turn to the right. See H539 (אָמַן).

H542.definition:
from H539 (אָמַן) (in the sense of training);
an expert
KJV: cunning workman.

H543.definition:
from H539 (אָמַן);
sure; abstract, faithfulness; adverb, truly
KJV: Amen, so be it, truth.

H545.definition:
feminine of H544 (אֹמֶן) (in the specific sense of training);
tutelage
KJV: brought up.

H546.definition:
feminine form of H544 (אֹמֶן) (in its usual sense);
adverb, surely
KJV: indeed.

H547.definition:
feminine active participle of H544 (אֹמֶן) (in the original sense of supporting);
a column
KJV: pillar.

H548.definition:
feminine of H543 (אָמֵן);
something fixed, i.e. a covenant. an allowance
KJV: certain portion, sure.

H549.definition:
the same as H548 (אֲמָנָה);
Amanah, a mountain near Damascus
KJV: Amana.

H550.definition:
or אֲמִינוֹן; from H539 (אָמַן); faithful;
Amnon (or Aminon), a son of David
KJV: Amnon.

H551.definition:
adverb from H544 (אֹמֶן);
verily
KJV: indeed, no doubt, surely, (it is, of a) true(-ly, -th).

H552.definition:
an orthographical variation of H551 (אׇמְנָם)
{verily}
KJV: in (very) deed; of a surety.

H553.definition:
a primitive root;
to be alert, physically (on foot) or mentally (in courage)
KJV: confirm, be courageous (of good courage, stedfastly minded, strong, stronger), establish, fortify, harden, increase, prevail, strengthen (self), make strong (obstinate, speed).

H554.definition:
probably from H553 (אָמַץ);
of a strong color, i.e. red (others fleet)
KJV: bay.

H557.definition:
from H553 (אָמַץ); strong;
Amtsi, an Israelite
KJV: Amzi.

H558.definition:
or אֲמַצְיָהוּ; from H553 (אָמַץ) and H3050 (יָהּ); strength of Jah;
Amatsjah, the name of four Israelites
KJV: Amaziah.

H559.definition:
a primitive root;
to say (used with great latitude)
KJV: answer, appoint, avouch, bid, boast self, call, certify, challenge, charge, [phrase] (at the, give) command(-ment), commune, consider, declare, demand, [idiom] desire, determine, [idiom] expressly, [idiom] indeed, [idiom] intend, name, [idiom] plainly, promise, publish, report, require, say, speak (against, of), [idiom] still, [idiom] suppose, talk, tell, term, [idiom] that is, [idiom] think, use (speech), utter, [idiom] verily, [idiom] yet.

H560.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H559 (אָמַר)
{to say (used with great latitude)}
KJV: command, declare, say, speak, tell.

H561.definition:
from H559 (אָמַר);
something said
KJV: answer, [idiom] appointed unto him, saying, speech, word.

H562.definition:
the same as H561 (אֵמֶר)
{something said}
KJV: promise, speech, thing, word.

H563.definition:
(Aramaic) perhaps from H560 (אֲמַר) (in the sense of bringing forth);
a lamb
KJV: lamb.

H564.definition:
from H559 (אָמַר); talkative;
Immer, the name of five Israelites
KJV: Immer.

H565.definition:
or אֶמְרָה; feminine of H561 (אֵמֶר), and meaning the same
{something said}
KJV: commandment, speech, word.

H566.definition:
from H564 (אִמֵּר);
Imri, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Imri.

H567.definition:
probably a patronymic from an unused name derived from H559 (אָמַר) in the sense of publicity, i.e. prominence; thus, a mountaineer;
an Emorite, one of the Canaanitish tribes
KJV: Amorite.

H568.definition:
or prolonged אֲמַרְיָהוּ; from H559 (אָמַר) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has said (i.e. promised);
Amarjah, the name of nine Israelites
KJV: Amariah.

H569.definition:
of uncertain (perhaps foreign) derivation;
Amraphel, a king of Shinar
KJV: Amraphel.

H571.definition:
contracted from H539 (אָמַן);
stability; (figuratively) certainty, truth, trustworthiness
KJV: assured(-ly), establishment, faithful, right, sure, true (-ly, -th), verity.

H572.definition:
from H4969 (מָתַח);
properly, something expansive, i.e. a bag
KJV: sack.

H573.definition:
from H571 (אֶמֶת); veracious;
Amittai, an Israelite
KJV: Amittai.

H574.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H4975 (מֹתֶן);
well-loined (i.e. burly) or mighty
KJV: terrible.

H575.definition:
or אָנָה; contracted from H370 (אַיִן);
where?; hence, whither?, when?; also hither and thither
KJV: [phrase] any (no) whither, now, where, whither(-soever).

H576.definition:
(Aramaic) or אֲנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H589 (אֲנִי)lemma אֲנַי second vowel, corrected to אֲנִי;
I
KJV: I, as for me.

H577.definition:
or אָנָּה; apparent contracted from H160 (אַהֲבָה) and H4994 (נָא);
oh now!
KJV: I (me) beseech (pray) thee, O.

H578.definition:
a primitive root;
to groan
KJV: lament, mourn.

H579.definition:
a primitive root (perhaps rather identical with H578 (אָנָה) through the idea of contraction in anguish);
to approach; hence, to meet in various senses
KJV: befall, deliver, happen, seek a quarrel.

H580.definition:
contracted for H587 (אֲנַחְנוּ);
we
KJV: we.

H581.definition:
(Aramaic) or (feminine) אִנִּיןlemma אֵנִּין first vowel, corrected to אִנִּין; (Aramaic), corresponding to H1992 (הֵם);
they
KJV: [idiom] are, them, these.

H582.definition:
from H605 (אָנַשׁ); properly, a mortal (and thus differing from the more dignified H120 (אָדָם)); hence,
a man in general (singly or collectively)
KJV: another, [idiom] (blood-) thirsty, certain, chap(-man); divers, fellow, [idiom] in the flower of their age, husband, (certain, mortal) man, people, person, servant, some ([idiom] of them), [phrase] stranger, those, [phrase] their trade. It is often unexpressed in the English versions, especially when used in apposition with another word. Compare H376 (אִישׁ).

H583.definition:
the same as H582 (אֱנוֹשׁ);
Enosh, a son of Seth
KJV: Enos.

H584.definition:
a primitive root;
to sigh
KJV: groan, mourn, sigh.

H585.definition:
from H585 (אֲנָחָה);
sighing
KJV: groaning, mourn, sigh.

H586.definition:
(Aramaic) or אֲנַחְנָה; (Aramaic), corresponding to H587 (אֲנַחְנוּ);
we
KJV: we.

H587.definition:
apparently from H595 (אָנֹכִי);
we
KJV: ourselves, us, we.

H588.definition:
probably from the same root as H5170 (נַחַר); a gorge or narrow pass;
Anacharath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Anaharath.

H589.definition:
contracted from H595 (אָנֹכִי);
I
KJV: I, (as for) me, mine, myself, we, [idiom] which, [idiom] who.

H590.definition:
probably from H579 (אָנָה) (in the sense of conveyance);
-a ship or (collectively) a fleet
KJV: galley, navy (of ships).

H591.definition:
feminine of H590 (אֳנִי);
a ship
KJV: ship(-men).

H592.definition:
from H578 (אָנָה);
groaning
KJV: lamentation, sorrow.

H593.definition:
from H578 (אָנָה) and H5971 (עַם); groaning of (the) people;
Aniam, an Israelite
KJV: Aniam.

H594.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to be narrow;
according to most a plumb-line, and to others a hook
KJV: plumb-line

H595.definition:
sometimes, ; a primitive pronoun;
I
KJV: I, me, [idiom] which.

H596.definition:
a primitive root;
to mourn, i.e. complain
KJV: complain.

H598.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H597 (אָנַס);
figuratively, to distress
KJV: trouble.

H599.definition:
a primitive root;
to breathe hard, i.e. be enraged
KJV: be angry (displeased).
